course: dictionary
lesson: 12667
title: Distal: far from the centre
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Distal is a science word, used in biology and medicine. It means further away from the centre of the body, or further from the point where something is joined on. Think of distant: distal sounds a little like it, and both mean far away.
explain: Doctors and nurses use distal to say exactly where something is. «The fingertips are distal to the elbow.» The fingertips are further from the centre of the body than the elbow, so they are distal to it. Ask yourself: is this part further out, or closer in?
explain: Distal has an opposite, proximal, which means closer to the centre of the body or the point of attachment. «The elbow is proximal to the fingertips.» Use the pair together and the meaning becomes clear.
fact: Distal means further from the centre of the body, or from the point where something is attached.
fact: Proximal is the opposite of distal: it means closer to the centre.
fact: «The fingertips are distal to the elbow.» Fingers are further out than the elbow.
fact: «The bandage went around the distal part of her arm, near the wrist.» The wrist is far from the body's centre.
fact: Distal is also used in geography for places far from a source, but in school science it usually means the body.
exercise: «The fingertips are distal to the elbow.» What does distal mean here? | Inside the elbow | Sore and red | *Further from the centre of the body than the elbow | Closer to the centre of the body than the elbow
exercise: What is the opposite of distal? | distant | distinct | *proximal | distort
exercise: «The cut was on the distal part of his arm, near his wrist.» Where was the cut? | On the back of the neck | Near the shoulder, close to the body | In the middle of the chest | *Far from the body, near the wrist
test: «The doctor said the injury was distal, in the fingers.» What does distal tell us? | Painful | Very large | Close to the heart | *Far from the centre of the body
test: Which part is more distal: the knee or the toes? | *Toes | Knee | Both are the same | Neither
exam: Compared with the shoulder, the wrist is ___. | central | near | proximal | *distal
